# /etc/layerx/kernel.env (0600 root), read by layerx-kernel.service.
# Provision /var/lib/layerx/kernel/layerx/node as a complete native paxd home
# owned by 4020:4020; home, config and data directories must be mode 0700.
# Required files: config/{genesis.json,config.toml,app.toml,node_key.json,
# priv_validator_key.json,receipt.key} and data/priv_validator_state.json.
# Private keys and signing state must be mode 0600. Provision the receipt
# signer in genesis; paxd validates the native genesis before every launch.
# Retain all data, sequencer WAL, keys and .committed-readiness.json on /data.
# Startup refuses an old standalone-daemon volume; it never resets it.
# Migration policy: retain the legacy volume offline, provision a separate
# native home, qualify committed state, then explicitly switch the mount.
# Do not copy legacy metadata, settlement or guarantor state into that home.

LAYERX_KERNEL_IMAGE=ghcr.io/sidiora-labs/layerx-kernel:<12-hex sha>
LAYERX_KERNEL_PROFILE=native
LAYERX_NODE_NETWORK_ID=125
LAYERX_NODE_EVM_CHAIN_ID=125
LAYERX_KERNEL_NODE_HOME=/data/layerx/node

# Both full and native select the shared in-process kernel in paxd.
# Node peers/seeds and consensus mode come from config/config.toml; native
# module state and the hyperpax_125-1 identity come from config/genesis.json.
# Root EVM RPC/WS: host loopback 8545/8546; P2P: 26656; readiness: 9460/readyz.
# The gateway owns authenticated public TLS and tenant API projection.
# LAYERX_NODE_NETWORK_ID is a domain policy id, not an EVM chain selector.
# LAYERX_NODE_EVM_CHAIN_ID and historical LAYERX_NODE_PAXEER_CHAIN_ID must
# both be 125 when supplied. Human/KMS services use their own service image
# and chain-id-only registry file; this entrypoint does not project that file.
# Public peer selection belongs to the gateway/client deployment, not node
# readiness: use HTTPS at /, verify the TLS name/CA and use distinct peers.
# Public names: api1.mainnet-beta.paxeer.network through
# api14.mainnet-beta.paxeer.network, plus api-mainnet-beta.paxeer.network.
# api15/api16 are retired public names. No public RPC name or NETWORK_NAME
# is required by either kernel profile; readiness reads only the local node.
